# Frontend architecture

Keep `app/page.tsx` small. Use the smallest practical Client Component boundary. Network and domain logic do not live inside JSX-heavy page components.

Favor composition over giant prop/state components. Separate components by responsibility. Preserve the existing visual identity unless a task explicitly requests a redesign.

## Preferred boundaries

Create a file when it has a real responsibility. Do not create files merely to satisfy this tree.

`components/soccer-analyst/`

- `SoccerAnalystClient.tsx`, `QueryForm.tsx`, `ThinkingTimeline.tsx`, `ResultView.tsx`
- `MatchCard.tsx`, `AnalysisPanel.tsx`, `SourceList.tsx`, `HighlightsSection.tsx`, `DeepAnalysis.tsx`

`lib/api/` — `types.ts`, `client.ts`, `sse.ts`, `errors.ts`, `config.ts`

`hooks/useSoccerQuery.ts` is appropriate for query lifecycle and state.

## Rendering

- Render according to `intent` and evidence state. Non-match intents (standings, fixtures, team news, transfer news, player info, statistics) must not be treated as failed match queries.
- Show a score card only for valid verified or scheduled match metadata. Never invent "Today", "Full Time", "Final", or "Live".
- Sources display `title` / `domain` / `url` from structured `sources[]` objects.
- Hide the highlights section when `highlights[]` is empty.
- Only allow HTTPS YouTube or YouTube-nocookie URLs in an iframe. Unsupported hosts render as normal external links. Iframes must have a `title`.
- External links opened in a new tab use appropriate `rel` (`noopener noreferrer`).
- Unknown team logos get a deterministic fallback (initials or placeholder), not a broken image.
- Deep analysis is an explicit control after sufficient verified evidence. Do not auto-call `/analyze`.

## Accessibility

- Controls have accessible labels. Toggles use correct button or switch semantics.
- Keyboard operation and visible focus states are required.
